<section class="media-object" id="media_object_2">
    <div class="media-object__inner">
                    <h2 class="left">What is a Distribution Board Upgrade?</h2>
                <div class="media-object__rows">
                                                <div class="media-object__row standard mobile-text-first">
                        <div class="media-object__column--content">
                            
<section class="full-width-content tbbi-wysiwyg-content">
    <blockquote><p><span data-contrast="auto">Distribution boards, commonly known as consumer units, breaker panels, fuse boards, and electric panels, are the origin of electrical systems. They house protective devices including circuit breakers (sometimes known as fuses) or switches for a site.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="auto">If you’ve been advised following an </span><a href="https://besgroup.com/services/electrical/eicr/"><span data-contrast="none">Electrical Installation Condition Report</span></a><span data-contrast="auto"> (EICR) inspection or power supply analysis that you require a distribution board replacement, you’ll also need to have residual current protection. Residual Current Devices (RCD) play a pivotal role in protecting electrical circuits, preventing direct contact electrical shocks.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}"> </span></p></blockquote>
</section>                        </div>
                        <div class="media-object__column--image">
                                                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2023/10/Electrical-Install-projects-Distribution-board-upgrades-4-min-scaled.jpg" alt="" />
                                                    </div>
                    </div>
                                    </div>
    </div>
</section>
<div class="client-logos-block" id="client_logos_block_3">
    <div class="client-logos-block__inner js-client-logos-block">
        <p>Who we've partnered with...</p>
        <div>
                                <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2025/02/SGRE-logo-edited-1.png" alt="Siemens Games Logo in black and white" />
                                                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2024/12/nhs-logo.png" alt="NHS company logo in black and white" />
                                                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2025/02/waterstones-logo-edited-1.png" alt="Waterstones company logo in black and white" />
                                                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2025/02/Wessex_Water-logo-edited-1.png" alt="Wessex Water Logo in black and white" />
                                                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2025/02/JCB-–-Logo-edited-1.png" alt="JCB company logo in black and white" />
                                            </div>
    </div>
</div>
<section class="benefits-block" id="benefits_block_4">
    <div class="benefits-block__inner">
                    <h2>Key benefits of Electrical Power Distribution Board Upgrades </h2>
                <div class="benefits-block__grid">
                            <div class="benefits-block__card">
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--icon">
                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2023/12/BECCBF1.png" alt="An icon of a cogwheel" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--content">
                        <p>Improved safety</p>
                        <p>An upgraded distribution board will meet current electrical safety standards which can help to prevent electrical fires and other hazards. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                                            <div class="benefits-block__card">
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--icon">
                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2025/02/Dark-Green-icon-Rocket-to-showcase-improvement-of-efficiency.png" alt="Black rocket icon" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--content">
                        <p>Increased efficiency</p>
                        <p>An upgraded distribution board can help to improve the efficiency of your electrical system old boards with corroded or loose connections can cause heat build up, volt drop and energy loss.   </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                                            <div class="benefits-block__card">
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--icon">
                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2023/12/BESGRO3.png" alt="Quality checklist icon" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--content">
                        <p>Compliance with regulations</p>
                        <p>In some cases, upgrading your distribution board may be required to comply with local electrical regulations. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                                            <div class="benefits-block__card">
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--icon">
                        <img src="https://besgroup.com/app/uploads/2025/02/Dark-Green-icon-Rocket-to-showcase-improvement-of-efficiency.png" alt="Black rocket icon" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefits-block__card--content">
                        <p>Supports scaling of electrical operations  </p>
                        <p>Distribution board upgrades, along with power supply upgrades, may also be required to support larger installations or new additions to your business such as EV chargers. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                                    </div>
    </div>
</section>
