<section class="tabbed-block js-tabbed-block dark" id="tabbed_block_15">
    <div class="tabbed-block__inner">
        <div class="tabbed-block__upper">
                            <h2>Electrical Panel Repairs & Upgrades by Sector</h2>
                                </div>
        <div class="tabbed-block__lower js-tab-container">
            <ul class="tabbed-block__tabs--desktop js-tabs">
                                    <li class="js-tab-trigger active" data-tab="0">Commercial Offices & Retail Buildings</li>
                                    <li class="js-tab-trigger " data-tab="1">Healthcare & Critical Facilities</li>
                                    <li class="js-tab-trigger " data-tab="2">Industrial, Manufacturing & Logistics</li>
                            </ul>
            <div class="tabbed-block__content">
                                                            <div class="tabbed-block__content--block js-tab-content" data-content="0">
                                                                                                
<section class="full-width-content tbbi-wysiwyg-content">
    <p><span style="font-weight: 300;">Many organisations undertake electrical panel upgrades for commercial buildings when older boards cannot provide the sufficient circuit capacity needed to support modern equipment. This is especially true in commercial offices where the use of IT equipment has increased significantly in the last decade or so. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">Through targeted office electrical panel repair services, office facilities managers can address issues such as overheating terminals or deteriorating protective devices before they escalate and cause material issues that affect business tenants. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">For </span><a href="https://besgroup.com/sectors/building-properties-and-real-estate/"><span style="font-weight: 300;">customer-facing properties such as retail buildings</span></a><span style="font-weight: 300;">, owners often rely on experienced retail store electrical panel repair contractors who can replace ageing boards that were not designed to support modern trading hours and decorative lighting systems.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">When EV charging points are introduced to offices and retail spaces, an electrical panel upgrade for EV charger installation may also be necessary to accommodate increased load. Did you know we also offer <a href="https://besgroup.com/services/electrical/ev-maintenance/">EV charger maintenance for businesses</a> nationwide? </span></p>
</section>                                                                                    </div>
                                            <div class="tabbed-block__content--block js-tab-content" data-content="1">
                                                                                                
<section class="full-width-content tbbi-wysiwyg-content">
    <p><span style="font-weight: 300;">Estates teams may commission hospital distribution board upgrades where legacy boards require modern RCD or RCBO integration to meet current safety standards. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">In </span><a href="https://besgroup.com/sectors/healthcare/"><span style="font-weight: 300;">healthcare settings</span></a><span style="font-weight: 300;">, panel upgrades are often phased to maintain supply continuity while enhancing protection against fault currents and equipment failure.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">Across all critical facilities, upgrading this distribution infrastructure strengthens resilience to support future capacity requirements and reduce reliance on outdated components that bring with them unnecessary risk.</span></p>
</section>                                                                                    </div>
                                            <div class="tabbed-block__content--block js-tab-content" data-content="2">
                                                                                                
<section class="full-width-content tbbi-wysiwyg-content">
    <p><span style="font-weight: 300;">Production facilities frequently require electrical panel upgrades, especially in factories, when machinery expansion and wider company growth push existing distribution systems beyond what they were originally designed for.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">Specialist industrial electrical panel repair contractors, such as the ones at BES Group, often work with </span><a href="https://besgroup.com/sectors/manufacturing/"><span style="font-weight: 300;">manufacturing firms</span></a><span style="font-weight: 300;"> to rectify damaged busbars or upgrade protection arrangements within high-load environments where sustained current demand increases thermal stress. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;"><a href="https://besgroup.com/sectors/transport-logistics-and-distribution-centres/">Logistics sites</a> may undertake warehouse electrical panel repair services where distribution boards support automation systems, loading bays and high-bay lighting operations across long shifts.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 300;">And in operationally sensitive settings where accuracy is critical, data centre electrical panel upgrades often take place because panel modifications must align with redundancy planning and minimise disruption to live infrastructure.</span></p>
</section>                                                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
            <ul class="tabbed-block__tabs--mobile">
                                                            <li>
                            <a class="js-mob-tab-trigger">
